# backend/.dockerignore (SPEC blocker B5): keep local secrets and runtime data out of any
# build whose context is backend/. Since blocker B3 the repository builds one image from the
# root Dockerfile (context: the repository root, which uses the root .dockerignore), and no
# compose file builds from this directory any more. The file stays as a guard for a direct
# `docker build backend/`.

.git
.venv
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
*.log

# secrets and keys (the example file is allowed back in)
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/.secret_key

# runtime data: trained models and user uploads never belong in an image
models
**/models
uploads
**/uploads
